WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.660
- You have a disability
insurance claim with Prudential.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.720
Here's three secrets they're
not going to tell you.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.060 align:start position:0% line:0%
I'm John Tucker, I'm
a disability attorney,

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.490 align:start position:0% line:0%
and I've been fighting
Prudential for my clients

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.300 size:78% position:39% line:0%
for nearly three decades.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.710
There's three things that come up

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.250
that my clients never knew about

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.710 line:0%
that I think you should know about.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.960 line:0%
First, Prudential is going to use doctors

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.900 align:start position:0% line:0%
in the background that you're
never going to talk to.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.380 line:0%
They're going to review your file

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.870 size:88% position:44% line:0%
and give Prudential opinions

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.290 line:0%
that they'll rely upon to deny your claim.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.530 line:0%
Those doctors may even call your doctors

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.890 line:0%
to have conversations about you,

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.520 align:start position:0% line:0%
that you won't find out
about until after the fact.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.620 line:0%
Tell your doctors not to talk to them,

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.603 align:start position:0% line:0%
and to ask for any questions
to be sent in writing.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.970 line:0%
Second, Prudential can be notorious

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.270 line:0%
for taking too long to decide claims.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.700 align:start position:0% line:0%
Group disability claims
have certain deadlines

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.290 align:start position:0% line:0%
that apply to them.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.810 size:81% position:41% line:0%
At the initial claim level
and at the appeal level,

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.650 line:0%
there's different periods of time

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.710 line:0%
that the insurance company can take

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.870 line:0%
to decide the claim or decide the appeal.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.660 size:78% position:39% line:0%
Prudential won't tell you
what those deadlines are,

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.921 line:0%
and then they'll take too much time.

00:01:13.921 --> 00:01:16.670 align:start position:0% line:0%
But in reality, if they
take too much time,

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.600 size:81% position:41% line:0%
you actually can go to the
next step in the process.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.280 line:0%
Sometimes that's filing a lawsuit,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.730 size:84% position:42% line:0%
and that's to your benefit,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.500 size:84% position:42% line:0%
but they won't tell you you
have the option to do that.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.010 line:0%
Finally, beware of Prudential
cherry-picking information

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.980 align:start position:0% line:0%
from your records that
helps them and hurts you.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.150 align:start position:0% line:0%
What that means is they'll
reach into your records

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.130 align:start position:0% line:0%
and pull out the facts
that help them deny you,

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.750 line:0%
but they won't pull out the facts

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.200 line:0%
that explain why you're disabled,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start position:0% line:0%
your symptoms, your
limitations, your restrictions.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.370 align:start position:0% line:0%
They'll ignore those.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.300 align:start position:0% line:0%
So when you get a decision
letter from Prudential,

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.550 line:0%
oftentimes you'll read it and
think, who is this person?

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.150 line:0%
Where are all the facts about me?

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.230 size:88% position:44% line:0%
Didn't they read my records?

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.410 line:0%
If you've been denied by Prudential,

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.920 align:start position:0% line:0%
give me a call at the
number on your screen below.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.890 line:0%
I represent people just like
you all over the United States,

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.680 align:start position:0% line:0%
from Florida to Alaska,

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.680 line:0%
in these group disability insurance cases.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.100 line:0%
Thanks for watching, I'm John Tucker.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.683
(upbeat music)

